course: dictionary
lesson: 3721
title: Flightless birds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Flightless» is built from two parts. Flight means flying, and -less means without, so flightless means without flying, or not able to fly. Look at the parts to work out a word you don't know.
explain: Flightless is used for birds and insects that have wings but cannot fly. «The kiwi of New Zealand is a flightless night bird» tells you the kiwi is a bird that cannot fly, even though it has wings.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «The cassowary is a big flightless bird with a crest» still makes sense if you read it as "a big bird that cannot fly with a crest on its head." If the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is probably right.
fact: Flightless means not able to fly.
fact: Flightless birds include the ostrich, emu, kiwi, penguin, cassowary and the dodo.
fact: «The dodo was a big flightless pigeon from Mauritius», and it was last reliably seen in 1662.
fact: Many flightless birds lived where there were few predators, so they never needed to fly away from danger.
exercise: «The kiwi of New Zealand is a flightless night bird.» What does flightless mean? | Able to fly very fast | Afraid of the dark | *Not able to fly | Very large
exercise: Which of these is a flightless bird? | Swallow | *Ostrich | Eagle | Robin
exercise: Which describes flightless insects? | Insects that swim fast | Insects that have no wings | *Insects that have wings but cannot fly | Insects that glow at night
test: «The cassowary is a big flightless bird with a crest.» What does flightless tell you about the cassowary? | It eats only fish | It lives in the sea | *It cannot fly | It is very tiny
test: Which bird from the sentences was last reliably seen in 1662? | Kiwi | *Dodo | Cassowary | Emu
exam: «Haast's eagle hunted moa, giant flightless birds much heavier than itself.» Which word tells you the moa could not fly? | *Flightless | Hunted | Heavier | Giant
